Based on the search results, the most recent Volkswagen Passat in the US market was the 2022 model year, which was the final year of production for the US-market Passat (Source 1, 11). The trim levels offered for the 2022 Passat were SE, R-Line, and Limited Edition (Source 1, 10, 11). There is no specific "T" trim listed.

However, the engine is consistently referred to as the "2.0T" engine, indicating a 2.0-liter Turbocharged engine (Source 1, 2, 5, 11). It is highly likely that the user's query for the "T" trim is a misunderstanding and they are referring to a model equipped with the standard 2.0T engine, possibly the base SE trim which is the entry-level model with this engine (Source 1).

Given that "T" is not a recognized trim level for the most recent Passat, and the engine designation "2.0T" is common across the range, I will evaluate based on the specifications of the base 2022 Volkswagen Passat SE trim, as this is the most likely interpretation of the user's request for a "Passat T".

